{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Until the morrow of the seventh sabbath you shall count.</b> You already know that the counting is only forty-nine, and therefore you will find a reason for the word תספרו — it is not attached to the word חמשים; rather, חמשים is attached to מקרבכם, for the counting is forty-nine and the offering is on the fiftieth day. Because the Torah did not mention the festival of Shavuot independently like the other festivals, saying for example 'in the third month, on the sixth of it, is the festival of Shavuot,' just as it said concerning Pesach, 'on the fifteenth day of this month is the festival of matzot' — this comes to teach that it is a festival drawn along after the command of the omer. And the forty-nine days of counting between the first day of Pesach and Shavuot — they are like the intermediate days of the festival (חולו של מועד) between the first day of Sukkot and Shemini Atzeret."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:46.538526520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}